  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sagar Singh vs State Of U.P. on 19 November, 2020 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth",
    "facts": "The instant Anticipatory Bail Application has been filed with a prayer to grant an anticipatory bail to the applicant, namely, Sagar Singh, in Case Crime No. 977 of 2020, under Section 272 I.P.C. and section 60 of U.P. Excise Act , Police Station - Shahpur, District - Gorakhpur. Submission is that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under section 272, I.P.C. is unjustified. Offence under section Sagar Singh vs State Of U.P. on 19 November, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/40416242/ 1 60 of Excise Act is bailable and triable by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged. The applicant has no criminal history to his credit. Applicant has definite apprehension of his arrest by the police. Learned AGA has opposed the prayer for anticipatory bail of the applicant.",
    "arguments": "Without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case and considering the nature of accusation and his antecedents, the applicant is entitled to be released on anticipatory bail in this case for the limited period considering the exception considered by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of Sushila Aggarwal Vs. State (NCT of Delhi)-2020 SCC Online SC 98.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case and considering the nature of accusation and his antecedents, the applicant is entitled to be released on anticipatory bail in this case for the limited period considering the exception considered by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of Sushila Aggarwal Vs. State (NCT of Delhi)-2020 SCC Online SC 98."
